  "notes": "{抱|だ}く means to hold someone or something in one's arms, typically embracing warmly.\n\nTRANSITIVITY:\n- Type: {他動詞|たどうし} (transitive)\n- Passive: {抱|だ}かれる (to be held/embraced)\n\nREADINGS:\n- {抱|だ}く: to physically hold/embrace (common, spoken)\n- {抱|いだ}く: to harbor feelings, to hold in one's heart (literary)\n\nASPECT (ている):\n{抱|だ}いている indicates the ongoing state of holding something: {子供|こども}を{抱|だ}いている (is holding a child).\n\nCOMMON PATTERNS:\n- {子供|こども}を{抱|だ}く: to hold a child\n- {強|つよ}く{抱|だ}く: to embrace tightly\n- {優|やさ}しく{抱|だ}く: to hold gently\n- {枕|まくら}を{抱|だ}いて{寝|ね}る: to sleep hugging a pillow\n\nRELATED:\n- {抱|だ}きしめる: to hug tightly\n- {抱|だ}っこ: being held (child's word)",
